{
  "title": "Checkers",
  "players": [{ "card": "player_red" }, { "card": "player_white" }],
  "comment": "English draughts. The board layer already had everything the moves need: the jump takes the piece it flies past because a pattern is also a scope and the anchor follows the piece, so 'down_right' read from the square landed on names the victim. What the game had to invent is the chain — a route back to the same seat while a piece is mid-jump. 'aims:<ability>' is how many cards one of this card's own abilities could point at right now, and a computed tag is asked once per card, so 'can_jump' worn by a piece is that piece having a jump and 'tagged:can_jump@mine.board' is a jump being on offer anywhere on my side. That is forced capture; and the same tag under 'chaining' is 'chain_open', which ends the chain the moment the jumps run out, so the game needs no button saying so. See ideas/01-boardgames.md.",
  "assets": {
    "man": { "per_player": ["circle:crimson:none", "circle:white:none"] },
    "king": { "per_player": ["star:crimson:none", "star:white:none"] }
  },
  "styles": {
    "piece": { "hide": ["title", "border", "plate"] },
    "draughtboard": { "hide": ["cell_outline"], "fit": "fill", "ratio": "grid", "chequer": ["#7a5230", "#e8d3a9"] }
  },
  "patterns": {
    "up_left": { "vectors": [[-1, 1]] },
    "up_right": { "vectors": [[1, 1]] },
    "down_left": { "vectors": [[-1, -1]] },
    "down_right": { "vectors": [[1, -1]] },
    "leap_up_left": { "vectors": [[-2, 2]] },
    "leap_up_right": { "vectors": [[2, 2]] },
    "leap_down_left": { "vectors": [[-2, -2]] },
    "leap_down_right": { "vectors": [[2, -2]] }
  },
  "computed_tags": {
    "jump_fl": { "needs": ["aims:jump_left >= 1"] },
    "jump_fr": { "needs": ["aims:jump_right >= 1"] },
    "jump_bl": { "needs": ["aims:jump_back_left >= 1"] },
    "jump_br": { "needs": ["aims:jump_back_right >= 1"] },
    "can_jump": { "any_of": ["jump_fl", "jump_fr", "jump_bl", "jump_br"] },
    "chain_open": { "needs": ["chaining@self >= 1", "tagged:can_jump@self"] }
  },
  "zones": [
    {
      "key": "board",
      "layout": "grid",
      "use": "abilities",
      "grid": [8, 8],
      "pos": [0.28, 0.03, 0.72, 0.97],
      "tags": ["draughtboard"]
    },
    {
      "key": "taken",
      "label": "Taken",
      "layout": "stack",
      "copies": "per_seat",
      "pos": [[0.76, 0.65, 0.97, 0.95], [0.76, 0.05, 0.97, 0.35]]
    },
    {
      "key": "seat_box", "status": "board", "layout": "stack", "copies": "per_seat",
      "pos": [[0.02, 0.65, 0.23, 0.95], [0.02, 0.05, 0.23, 0.35]]
    },
    { "key": "rules", "layout": "stack", "pos": [0.78, 0.40, 0.95, 0.58] }
  ],
  "phases": [
    {
      "key": "red_move",
      "type": "player_input",
      "label": "Red to move",
      "seat": "next",
      "on_enter": ["stat_set:chaining@each.anyone.piece:0"],
      "next": [
        { "when": "count:piece@enemy.board == 0", "then": "red_won" },
        { "when": "tagged:chain_open@mine.board", "then": "red_move", "seat": "same" },
        { "then": "white_move" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "white_move",
      "type": "player_input",
      "label": "White to move",
      "seat": "next",
      "on_enter": ["stat_set:chaining@each.anyone.piece:0"],
      "next": [
        { "when": "count:piece@enemy.board == 0", "then": "white_won" },
        { "when": "tagged:chain_open@mine.board", "then": "white_move", "seat": "same" },
        { "then": "red_move" }
      ]
    },
    { "key": "red_won", "type": "automatic", "actions": ["reveal:red_wins"] },
    { "key": "white_won", "type": "automatic", "actions": ["reveal:white_wins"] }
  ],
  "end_conditions": [],
  "setup": {
    "place": [
      { "card": "player_red", "zone": "seat_box" },
      { "card": "player_white", "zone": "seat_box" },
      {
        "card": "man",
        "owner": "player_red",
        "zone": "board",
        "at": ["a1", "c1", "e1", "g1", "b2", "d2", "f2", "h2", "a3", "c3", "e3", "g3"]
      },
      {
        "card": "man",
        "owner": "player_white",
        "zone": "board",
        "at": ["b6", "d6", "f6", "h6", "a7", "c7", "e7", "g7", "b8", "d8", "f8", "h8"]
      },
      { "card": "how_to_play", "zone": "rules" }
    ]
  },
  "cards": [
    { "key": "player_red", "text": "Red", "tags": ["red_side"] },
    { "key": "player_white", "text": "White", "tags": ["white_side"] },
    {
      "key": "man",
      "text": "Man",
      "asset": "man",
      "tooltip": "One square diagonally forward, onto an empty square — but only while nothing of yours can jump, because a jump on offer must be taken. It jumps an enemy piece to the empty square beyond it, and goes on jumping as long as jumps are there. Reaching the far row crowns it, and the crowning ends the move.",
      "tags": ["piece", "man"],
      "comment": "One ability per jump direction, because the action has to name the square it flew over and only the rule that chose that direction knows which one that is. The gate is the same on all of them: 'chaining' is 1 on a piece in the middle of a chain, so max:chaining over my side is 0 while nobody is mid-jump (everyone matches) and 1 once somebody is (only they match). A step is gated the other way round, on nothing of mine having a jump, which is the rulebook making a capture compulsory.",
      "card_stats": { "rank": 0, "chaining": 0 },
      "challenge": {
        "needs": ["rank@self == 8"],
        "pass": ["transform:self:king", "stat_set:chaining@each.mine.piece:0"],
        "fail": []
      },
      "abilities": [
        {
          "key": "step",
          "text": "Move",
          "needs": ["not_tagged:can_jump@mine.board"],
          "moves": [{ "patterns": ["up_left", "up_right"], "fill": "empty" }],
          "action": ["move_to:target", "resolve_challenge", "end_phase"]
        },
        {
          "key": "jump_left",
          "text": "Jump left",
          "needs": ["max:chaining@mine.board == chaining@self"],
          "moves": [{ "patterns": ["leap_up_left"], "fill": "empty", "where": ["tagged:piece@enemy.down_right"] }],
          "action": [
            "move_to:target",
            "move:enemy.down_right:taken",
            "stat_set:chaining@self:1",
            "resolve_challenge",
            "end_phase"
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "jump_right",
          "text": "Jump right",
          "needs": ["max:chaining@mine.board == chaining@self"],
          "moves": [{ "patterns": ["leap_up_right"], "fill": "empty", "where": ["tagged:piece@enemy.down_left"] }],
          "action": [
            "move_to:target",
            "move:enemy.down_left:taken",
            "stat_set:chaining@self:1",
            "resolve_challenge",
            "end_phase"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "king",
      "text": "King",
      "asset": "king",
      "tooltip": "One square diagonally, forward or back, and it jumps in all four directions. A jump on offer must be taken, and it goes on jumping as long as jumps are there.",
      "tags": ["piece", "king"],
      "card_stats": { "rank": 0, "chaining": 0 },
      "abilities": [
        {
          "key": "step",
          "text": "Move",
          "needs": ["not_tagged:can_jump@mine.board"],
          "moves": [{ "patterns": ["up_left", "up_right", "down_left", "down_right"], "fill": "empty" }],
          "action": ["move_to:target", "end_phase"]
        },
        {
          "key": "jump_left",
          "text": "Jump forward left",
          "needs": ["max:chaining@mine.board == chaining@self"],
          "moves": [{ "patterns": ["leap_up_left"], "fill": "empty", "where": ["tagged:piece@enemy.down_right"] }],
          "action": ["move_to:target", "move:enemy.down_right:taken", "stat_set:chaining@self:1", "end_phase"]
        },
        {
          "key": "jump_right",
          "text": "Jump forward right",
          "needs": ["max:chaining@mine.board == chaining@self"],
          "moves": [{ "patterns": ["leap_up_right"], "fill": "empty", "where": ["tagged:piece@enemy.down_left"] }],
          "action": ["move_to:target", "move:enemy.down_left:taken", "stat_set:chaining@self:1", "end_phase"]
        },
        {
          "key": "jump_back_left",
          "text": "Jump back left",
          "needs": ["max:chaining@mine.board == chaining@self"],
          "moves": [{ "patterns": ["leap_down_left"], "fill": "empty", "where": ["tagged:piece@enemy.up_right"] }],
          "action": ["move_to:target", "move:enemy.up_right:taken", "stat_set:chaining@self:1", "end_phase"]
        },
        {
          "key": "jump_back_right",
          "text": "Jump back right",
          "needs": ["max:chaining@mine.board == chaining@self"],
          "moves": [{ "patterns": ["leap_down_right"], "fill": "empty", "where": ["tagged:piece@enemy.up_left"] }],
          "action": ["move_to:target", "move:enemy.up_left:taken", "stat_set:chaining@self:1", "end_phase"]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "key": "how_to_play",
      "text": "How to play",
      "tags": ["immutable"],
      "play": { "phases": [] },
      "tooltip": "Click one of your pieces to light up the squares it can reach, then click a square to move. A piece that can jump two ways asks which.\n\nMen move one square diagonally forward. A jump takes the piece flown over and lands beyond it. A man reaching the far row is crowned a king, which moves and jumps in all four directions.\n\nA jump on offer must be taken, so while any of your pieces can jump, none of them may step. A jump does not end your turn either: the piece goes on jumping until it has no jump left, and then the turn passes by itself.\n\nNot implemented yet:\n- Losing when you cannot move. You lose by running out of pieces only.\n- Draws.\n- Flying kings, which belong to international draughts rather than to this one."
    },
    {
      "key": "red_wins",
      "text": "Red wins",
      "story": "White has nothing left on the board.",
      "play": { "action": ["load_game:menu.json"] }
    },
    {
      "key": "white_wins",
      "text": "White wins",
      "story": "Red has nothing left on the board.",
      "play": { "action": ["load_game:menu.json"] }
    }
  ]
}
